.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_POESCHL_TELLER "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_poeschl_teller (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_poeschl_teller \- compute eigenstates of a Poeschl-Teller potential hole.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_poeschl_teller
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a Poeschl\-\-Teller potential profile and finds eigenstates analytically.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-a\fR [ \fB\-\-widthparameter\fR ] arg (=0.1) Width parameter [1/angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-l\fR [ \fB\-\-depthparameter\fR ] arg (=2)
Depth parameter.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR [ \fB\-\-length\fR ] arg (=300)
Length of potential profile [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-mass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Effective mass (relative to free
electron).
.TP
\fB\-N\fR [ \fB\-\-nz\fR ] arg (=301)
Number of spatial points for output file.
.TP
\fB\-\-nstmax\fR arg (=0)
Maximum number of subbands to find.  The
default (0) means that all states will be
found up to maximum confining potential.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or
\&'l', for electrons, heavy holes or light
holes respectively.
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Output files
   'E*.r'    Energy of each state:
             Column 1: state index.
             Column 2: energy [meV].

   'wf_*i.r' Wave function amplitude at each position:
             Column 1: position [m]
             Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

   'v.r'     Confining potential:
             Column 1: Spatial location [m]
             Column 2: Potential [J]

In each case, the '*' is replaced by the particle ID and the 'i' is replaced by the number of the state.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the potential and eigenstates for Poeschl--Teller hole with depth parameter 2, and width parameter 0.05/angstrom:
    qwwad_ef_poeschl_teller --widthparameter 0.05 --depthparameter 2

Compute solutions for a Poeschl--Teller hole with depth 2, width 0.1/angstrom and effective mass 0.1me:
    qwwad_ef_poeschl_teller --widthparameter 0.1 --mass 0.1 --depthparameter 2
